  "trial": "P-54",
  "question": "Can the Controller's installation token, narrowed to issues: read on the canary alone, read the issue a pull request is bound to, GET /repos/{repo}/issues/{n}, as the acceptance port's labelled() reads it; and what is a token with metadata: read alone answered for the same read?",
  "pass": "Written before the run, at the top of tools/trial_p54_issue_lookup.sh: pass if a token for the Controller's installation narrowed to issues: read, on the canary alone, reads GET /repos/{repo}/issues/{n} with 200, and the body is that issue: its number is the one asked, it holds no pull_request, and its labels are a list of objects each with a name, which is what labelled() reads. Fail otherwise. Recorded, deciding nothing: what a token with metadata: read alone is answered for the same read; the canary is public, so GitHub may answer it as it would anyone (decision 0068), and a private repo is not asked. Run at the Maintainer's terminal with the Controller's key, two tokens minted and revoked. Of each mint only what was asked and that it succeeded is kept: the script stops on any other answer.",
